# Use the subclass mock maker instead of Mockito's default inline mock maker.
#
# The inline maker self-attaches a Byte Buddy agent by spawning an external process. When that
# attach fails, Mockito throws from plugin initialisation — and because Spring Boot's
# ResetMocksTestExecutionListener touches Mockito before EVERY test, the entire suite errors with
# "Could not initialize inline Byte Buddy mock maker" even though nothing here mocks anything.
# It is intermittent, which is worse than a hard failure: green at home, red on the day.
#
# Verified: with this file removed and -XX:+DisableAttachMechanism, every test in the suite errors.
# With it, they all pass. Reproduce that check with:
#   ./mvnw -o clean test -DargLine="-XX:+DisableAttachMechanism"
#
# If you later need to stub a final class or a static method, delete this file and register
# Mockito as a real -javaagent rather than going back to self-attach.
mock-maker-subclass
